## Review & Understand

- The composer can target a project different from the chat's (`message.project_id`), already resolved in `Chat.vue` as `messageTargetProject` (`messageProject || chatProject`).
- `@mention` IntelliSense is still chat-only:
  - `runIntelliSense()` searches `this.chatProject?.$state.searchMentions(...)`.
  - `mentionList` resolves from the chat project state.
- Only the chat's project is initialized up front (`initProjectState(chatProject)`); every other project only has `$api` + an `UNINITIALIZED` `$state` (no `searchMentions`), so the target must be prepared on demand.

## Change Proposal

1. `runIntelliSense()` resolves the project through a new `resolveMentionProject()` helper (message project first, chat project as fallback), so `searchMentions` runs against the message's project.
2. `resolveMentionProject()` lazily calls `$projects.initProjectState(target)` when that project has no `searchMentions` yet (idempotent, no-op when already loaded).
3. `mentionList` follows the same target so mention chips are resolved against the message project.
4. A `messageProject` watcher drops stale suggestions when the target project changes.

## Changes Summary

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `src/components/chat/Chat.vue` | IntelliSense searches mentions in `message.project_id` (when present) instead of always the chat project; lazy project init, mention list alignment, stale-suggestion reset. |

