## Review & Understand

- A `Message` may carry its own `project_id` (targets a project other than the chat's working project). The composer picker already **displays** it when editing and lets the user pick another project (`messageTargetProject`).
- The **change is not persisted**: `updateMessage()` only sends `project_id` when the composer targets a *non-null* project:

  ```js
  if (this.messageProject?.project_id) update.project_id = this.messageProject.project_id
  ```

  Picking the chat's project sets `messageProject = null` → nothing is written → the old `project_id` silently stays on the message (and the `ChatEntry` badge stays until the next reload).

## Change Proposal

1. `Chat.vue` — add `messageProjectTouched` (set by `onMessageProjectChanged`, i.e. only when the user really uses the picker).
2. `updateMessage()` — write `project_id` (including `null`, which clears the override) whenever the selection was touched, instead of only when non-null. Untouched edits keep the stored value (`project_id: null` is no longer swallowed).
3. Reset the flag on [`onEditMessage`, `onResetEdit`, `cleanUserInputAndWaitAnswer`].
4. `src/model/chat.ts` — declare the optional `project_id` on `Message` (the field the whole feature relies on).

## Changes Summary

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `src/components/chat/Chat.vue` | Persists the project chosen while editing, including clearing it back to the chat's project; tracks picker usage with `messageProjectTouched`. |
| `src/model/chat.ts` | `Message.project_id?: string \| null` documented. |

